---
// The privacy notice. Short, because the site collects nothing itself.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { NAME, OWNER, EMAIL, LOCATION } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · Craig's Works"
  description="How Craig's Works handles personal information: what's collected, why, and your rights."
  path="privacy/"
>
  <article class="doc wrap" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <div class="tile">
      <h1 id="privacy-title">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="meta mono">Last updated October 2026</p>

      <h2>Who's responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {NAME} is the trading name of {OWNER}, a sole trader based in {LOCATION}, UK. {OWNER} is the controller of any personal
        information described here. Questions or requests: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies, runs no analytics or advertising, and loads nothing from other companies: its fonts and
        scripts are served from craigsworks.com itself. The one thing it remembers is a "pause animations" choice, kept in
        your own browser's storage and never sent anywhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub may keep technical logs of visits (such as IP
        addresses) to run and secure its service; see
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
          >GitHub's privacy statement</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>When you get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        If you email or book a call, I'll use your name, contact details and what you tell me to reply, arrange the call
        and, if we work together, to deliver and invoice the work. The lawful bases are taking steps towards a contract and
        my legitimate interest in answering enquiries. I keep enquiries that don't go anywhere for up to 12 months, and
        business records for as long as the law requires (six years for tax).
      </p>
      <p>I don't sell your information or use it for marketing, and I only share it where the law requires.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask for a copy of the information I hold about you, or ask me to correct or delete it, by emailing <a
          href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a
        >. If you're unhappy with how I've handled it, you can complain to the
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    padding-top: 72px;
    padding-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .tile {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding: clamp(28px, 5vw, 56px);
  }
  .tile:hover {
    transform: none;
    box-shadow: none;
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
  }
  .meta {
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 32px 0 10px;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--text);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }
</style>
